You should probably wish for a +2 gray dragon scale mail instead. Magic
resistance is really really important. Although the best set would probably
be with silver dragon scales and a cloak of magic resistance.

> How do I deal with all the traps in Gehennom?? I though levitation
> would work, but apparently they still go off. I REALLY don't want to
> destroy my robe setting off a random poly trap.

If your items are *proof, then the traps shouldn't hurt them. And if you
have magic resistance, then teleport, level teleport and poly traps will
not affect you.

> And what weapon should I use? I have been using Excalibur, since it
> stops the level drain from all the vamps, etc...But it makes demons
> pissed off. I can throw Mjollnir, or use the silver Werebane.

You should probably use the Mjollnir. If you have 25 st then
you can throw it and it will almost always return to your hand. Most
valkyries use it.

> What am I missing before I venture deeper??? What weapon should I use??
> And, most importantly, how do I keep all my armor from being destroyed
> by those damn traps that are everwhere?

You should probably genocide h and L to get rid of mind flayers, master
mind flayers and all liches. If you are a dwarf though, then you can't
genocide h or you'll die. You should also have a really low AC, somewhere
around -30 is enough. Donate to priests to get a low natural AC. 400*XL
will lover your AC. Remember to take off all armor you have before donating,
and remember to put them back on afterwards. The traps can't destroy your
armor if they are *proof. Of the demon lords that lie in Gehennom, I have
found Yeenoghu the most difficult one to handle, after Demogorgon of course.
He has no lair though, so you might not see him. Asmodeus is easy,
and if you have potions of healing, Juiblex can't really hurt you either.
I suggest you bribe the demon lords you don't have to kill. They can summon
rather nasty things. If you make it to Orcus' town, you should use a rubber
chicken to kill Orcus. That way you'll get his wand of death with almost
full gharges. 




